  "criticalFix": {
    "problem": "A Windows SDK launcher could finish or be cancelled while a child retained inherited output pipes; killing only the launcher left cleanup timing dependent on a helper child naturally exiting.",
    "implementation": "Finite Windows Go module/SDK commands now run through the bundled engine owner. The target is atomically assigned to a non-inherited Windows Job Object with KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE; IDE death closes the owner lifetime pipe. Unix keeps its existing PTY process-group ownership.",
    "regressionEvidence": "Windows raw go-race evidence contains PASS for all seven processowner tests, including completed-launcher orphan, owner kill, parent pipe EOF, and exact argument/environment/cwd/stdio/status preservation."
  },
